  "title": "Exact self-similar laws build finitely ramified spaces",
  "subject": "Which three-bit knots are exact counted fixed points of substitution by their own copies, and the towers their smallest single-scale gadgets build",
  "conclusion": "Up to six copies, the three-bit knots that reproduce themselves with uniform counts are parity, twisted not-all-equal and two three-excluded classes; not-all-equal does so at seven. Their towers keep the corner law at every scale with growth exponents log2 3, 2 and log3 7, but are finitely ramified, and softening is repelled at least threefold per level.",
